- op: create  # e8d3
  at: '2026-09-19T02:49:54Z'  # e8d3
  by: agent  # e8d3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e8d3
  clock: 1  # e8d3
  nonce: e8d3  # e8d3
  data:  # e8d3
    kind: invariant  # e8d3
    title: "scip/edges.py mints edge types 'has_type' and 'defined_by' that no registry declares, through a list-of-tuples the L1/L3 gates cannot see; no producer emits them today"  # e8d3
    status: violated  # e8d3
    priority: 3  # e8d3
    parent:  # e8d3
    tags:  # e8d3
    - scip  # e8d3
    - edge_type  # e8d3
    - axis  # e8d3
    isbefore: []  # e8d3
    duplicate_of: []  # e8d3
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e8d3
    pr_ref:  # e8d3
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-18 while measuring WI-zapuk on the recorded aardvark-dns fixture.\n\nscip/edges.py (the SymbolInformation.relationships -> Edge shim, WI-mafut Slice C) maps SCIP Relationship flags through\n\n    _RELATION_EDGE_TYPES = [(\"is_implementation\", \"implements\"), (\"is_type_definition\", \"has_type\"),\n                            (\"is_reference\", \"references\"), (\"is_definition\", \"defined_by\")]\n\n`implements` and `references` are registered edge types; `has_type` and `defined_by` are NOT (edge_types.all_edge_type_names() returns False for both). The value reaches Edge.create(edge_type=edge_type) through a variable, so the L3 producer gate (literal-string arguments) never sees it, and the L1 consumer gate reads frozensets/dicts named *EDGE_TYPE*, not a list of tuples named _RELATION_EDGE_TYPES — the same indirection shape WI-rorul (otp_call/otp_cast via dict) closed for one producer.\n\nNO PRODUCER TODAY: rust-analyzer 1.94.0 leaves `relationships` empty on every SymbolInformation (0 relationship edges on the recorded index), so the two values are minted by no run — a vocabulary value with no producer AND no registry entry. A scip-python or scip-typescript backend (WI-nanom) does populate relationships (is_implementation, is_type_definition), at which point the SCIP arm would emit an edge type no ADR-0023 consumer has a case for.\n\nFIX SHAPE (pick one per value, do not keep both): register `has_type` / `defined_by` in edge_types.py with an ADR-0023 axis classification, OR fold them onto registered values (is_type_definition -> the existing type-relation edge type if one is registered; is_definition -> drop, since a Definition relationship duplicates the Symbol itself). Then add a conformance test in the test_scip_kind_map_conformance.py shape: every value in _RELATION_EDGE_TYPES is a registered edge type, and the gate can fail."  # e8d3
    fields:  # e8d3
      statement: "Every edge_type a producer emits is a registered ADR-0023 value; a value reached through a variable or a list-of-tuples is subject to the same rule as a literal."  # e8d3
      root_cause: "scip/edges.py _RELATION_EDGE_TYPES maps SCIP Relationship flags to edge-type strings via a list of tuples; the L3 gate reads literal keyword arguments and the L1 gate reads *EDGE_TYPE*-named sets, so the indirection escaped both, and rust-analyzer emits no relationships so no run ever produced the unregistered values."  # e8d3
- op: discuss  # 1de5
  at: '2026-10-03T06:42:03Z'  # 1de5
  by: agent  # 1de5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1de5
  clock: 2  # 1de5
  nonce: 1de5  # 1de5
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). CURRENT; one claim corrected.\n- scip/edges.py:81-86 still maps relationship flags to has_type and defined_by; all_edge_type_names() returns False for both, and there is no registered type-relation edge type to fold into (closest: defines_target, instantiates). Edge.create(edge_type=\"has_type\") succeeds at runtime, and check-producer-axis-coherence reports 0 new leaks, confirming the gates cannot see these values.\n- \"No producer today\" still true for BOTH backends: rust-analyzer's recorded index has 0 relationships; scip-python 0.6.6 (shipped, WI-nanom; it does call scip_index_to_edges) has 0 in its recorded sample, and on a small inheritance fixture it emitted only is_implementation (6 relationships, 4 implements edges).\n- CORRECTION: \"scip-python ... does populate relationships (is_implementation, is_type_definition)\": is_type_definition was not observed.\n- SIDE OBSERVATION, not chased: scip-python reports a concrete subclass (Sq(Base)) and method overrides as is_implementation, so they become implements rather than extends."  # 1de5
- op: discuss  # 62e6
  at: '2026-10-03T09:15:47Z'  # 62e6
  by: agent  # 62e6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 62e6
  clock: 3  # 62e6
  nonce: '62e6'  # 62e6
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (concurrent run, not merged): branch jgstern-agent/fix/nakur, commit e489b683da (on top of WI-nakur's a56cc21c1b).\n\n- RED first: with WI-nakur's value_flow in place, test_live_tree_producer_axis_ratchet and test_no_strict_producer_violations_for_edge_type failed naming has_type and defined_by at scip/edges.py:133, and scripts/check-producer-axis-coherence exited 1 with the same two values. Before WI-nakur both gates were green with these values in the tree.\n- Fix: FOLD both onto `references` (is_type_definition, is_definition), flag kept on meta[\"scip_relationship_flag\"]; one edge per DISTINCT type per relationship (three flags now share `references`, and a second edge would repeat the id). Precedent: the TS analyzer carries a type reference as references + ast_type_ref. The description's \"drop is_definition, it duplicates the Symbol itself\" was not followed: SCIP relates a symbol to a different one there (from upstream scip.proto comments as recalled; only scip_pb2 is vendored, so not re-read).\n- Conformance gates (test_scip_edges.py::TestRelationMapConformance): every mapped value registered; map total over Relationship's bool fields; positive control rejects the pre-fix map.\n- GREEN after: ratchet + strict tests pass; check-producer-axis-coherence \"0 new leaks\".\n- ZERO MEASURED OUTPUT EFFECT: no recorded run produces either flag (premise audit 2026-10-03). The general statement (a value through a variable or list-of-tuples is subject to the registry) is held by the L3 ratchet only for the shapes value_flow follows; its refusals are listed on WI-gajoz-fasad-vojih-gomup-domar-zivis-durok-rudin."  # 62e6
