  message: "Merged in PR #1415 (dev 1a7fcbff88). Integration: commits reordered pubin -> dahuh -> nakur so every commit is green; CI needed a schema-coverage baseline entry for the five values registered as pending (corpus has no LuaJIT FFI / N-API / Clojure multimethod code).\n\nFixed on jgstern-agent/fix/nakur (e489b683da).\n\n- **Before** (with a56cc21c1b's gate): `test_no_strict_producer_violations_for_edge_type` and `check-producer-axis-coherence` (exit 1) both named has_type / defined_by at scip/edges.py:133. Before a56cc21c1b, no gate could see them.\n- **Fix:** `is_type_definition` and `is_definition` fold onto the registered `references`, with the flag kept in `meta[\"scip_relationship_flag\"]` and one edge per distinct type per relationship. New conformance tests (`TestRelationMapConformance`) check registration and totality, with a control that rejects the old map.\n- **After:** ratchet \"0 new leaks\".\n- **No measured output change:** neither flag appears in any recorded index.\n- **The general claim is held** by the L3 ratchet for the shapes value_flow follows. Its refusals are on WI-gajoz-fasad-vojih-gomup-domar-zivis-durok-rudin. NOT asserted beyond that.\n\n---"  # 6439
